| **Question Quality**             | Questions are unclear, irrelevant, or unstructured.   | Some relevant questions but several are confusing or off-topic. | Mostly clear and relevant questions with minor repetition. | Well-structured, focused questions aligned with the interview’s goal.     | Questions are clear, insightful, and effectively assess skills and fit.                              |
| **Active Listening & Follow-Up** | Ignores or skips over candidate responses.            | Acknowledges answers but rarely builds on them.                 | Listens adequately but follow-up is surface-level.         | Demonstrates attentive listening and asks thoughtful follow-up questions. | Consistently listens deeply, adapts questions based on answers, and keeps the conversation engaging. |
| **Structure & Flow**             | Interview feels disorganized or jumps between topics. | Some structure but lacks logical progression.                   | Reasonably organized with a few unclear transitions.       | Smooth and logical flow with clear topic transitions.                     | Interview is highly structured, natural, and easy for the candidate to follow.                       |
| **Professionalism & Fairness**   | Shows bias, impatience, or unprofessional tone.       | Occasionally unprofessional or dismissive.                      | Maintains a mostly professional and neutral tone.          | Professional and fair throughout, with respectful communication.          | Exemplary professionalism, neutrality, and inclusiveness at all times.                               |
| **Candidate Engagement**         | Makes the candidate feel uncomfortable or unwelcome.  | Provides minimal encouragement or acknowledgment.               | Keeps the conversation neutral but somewhat dry.           | Encourages the candidate and maintains a welcoming tone.                  | Creates a highly engaging, comfortable, and motivating interview experience.                         |

